  "name": "ASPERGILLUS - IgG ANTIBODY",
  "code": "2687",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>The assay detects IgG antibody against Aspergillus species, which are ubiquitous fungi. However, A.fumigatus, A.niger and A.clavatus can cause different diseases including hypersensitivity&nbsp;pneumonitis (HP), allergic bronchopulmonary aspergillosis (ABPA), pulmonary aspergilloma (fungus ball) and invasive aspergillosis (IA). The antibody response to A. Fumigatus antigens is&nbsp;polyclonal; however increasing IgG antibody titres were found to be correlated with active infection &amp; sometimes seem to precede the radiographic findings. Overall Sensitivity of the assay&nbsp;ranges from 90 to 93 %, however lower sensitivity is observed in immunocompromised individual with invasive aspergillosis. Rarely cross reactivity with other fungi like Alternaria tenuis and&nbsp;Cladosporium herbarum have been documented.</p>",
